cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this documentation template in academic work, teaching
  materials, or software engineering projects, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
  Documentation structure adapted from the FER Software Engineering course 
  template by Vlado Sruk, licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The application 
  and its content were created by the student team named above.
title: "Software Engineering Project Documentation Template"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sruk"
    given-names: "Vlado"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0411-3398"
    affiliation: "University of Zagreb, Faculty of Electrical Engineering and Computing"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
repository-code: "https://github.com/VladoSruk/Software-Engineering"
url: "https://github.com/VladoSruk/Software-Engineering"
license: "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0"
abstract: >-
  An open educational resource providing a standardized documentation
  structure for student software projects developed within the
  Software Engineering course at the Faculty of Electrical Engineering
  and Computing (FER), University of Zagreb. The template covers
  project description, requirements, deployment, installation,
  technology selection rationale, licensing, AI usage disclosure,
  teamwork reporting, and project governance.
keywords:
  - "software engineering"
  - "project documentation"
  - "README template"
  - "GitHub"
  - "software architecture"
  - "requirements engineering"
  - "project management"
  - "software testing"
  - "educational resource"
  - "open educational resources"
  - "AI usage policy"
